Description: link the networking classes through libbe, add Debian tinyxml
 On V\OS the net kit, the netservices stack and ColumnListView are all
 compiled into libbe (nm -D libbe.so shows BUrlRequest, NetEndpoint,
 BNetworkRoster and 115 ColumnListView symbols) and no package ships
 libbnetapi, libnetservices, libnetwork or libcolumnlistview, so the
 original LIBS line dies with "cannot find -lbnetapi" (and the rest).
 Dropping those four entries keeps every symbol resolving through the
 libbe that is already linked. tinyxml stays: it comes from Debian's
 libtinyxml-dev, which upstream's #include <tinyxml.h> and the TiXml
 calls in src/SearchForm.cpp need. The trailing m comes from the link
 error on sqrtf (MapsView.cpp): Debian's ld does not take libm
 transitively through libbe's own NEEDED, so libm has to be named.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Maps

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 #	- 	if your library does not follow the standard library naming scheme,
 #		you need to specify the path to the library and it's name.
 #		(e.g. for mylib.a, specify "mylib.a" or "path/mylib.a")
-LIBS = $(STDCPPLIBS) be bnetapi netservices shared translation tracker network columnlistview tinyxml
+LIBS = $(STDCPPLIBS) be shared translation tracker tinyxml m
 
 #	Specify additional paths to directories following the standard libXXX.so
 #	or libXXX.a naming scheme. You can specify full paths or paths relative
